    Enforce partVersion.kernel at compose time. When checkComposition
    evaluates parts against the release's kernel version, any declared
    range that does not satisfy the kernel is flagged as a fatal
    kernel_mismatch problem, refusing the composition.
    
    An absent range on a part is accepted without error to preserve backward
    compatibility for versions published before the field existed, and a
    kernel artifact has no kernel requirement of its own.
    
