    D3 landed scopedBy and nothing resolves a scope. api.service.ts says the cause
    outright -- 'the usual cause is a site with no authorize hook; the coarse gate
    cannot resolve a scope, only the site knows what an organization means to it'
    -- and bin/node.mjs configured none. So meta.user.tenant_id was always empty
    and every scopedBy collection refused every caller.
    
    The symptom is the tell: a correctly signed-in console got 200 from
    part.find and release.find and 401 from site.find, because site is the only
    scoped one of the three. Found by the first console to get past sign-in, which
    is the third time that sentence has been written about this repository -- the
    same shape as D3a, where adopting scopedBy broke the serving path because
    cdn.resolve_site called a now-scoped find.
    
    The hook treats a caller-supplied organization as a request rather than a
    grant: the x-organization header names one, membership is checked before it is
    honoured, and a non-member gets 404 rather than 403, because whether an
    organization exists is not something an unrelated caller confirms by probing.
    One membership needs no header; more than one without a header resolves no
    scope rather than guessing.
